      <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
      <description><![CDATA[<!DOCTYPE html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><style>html{color-scheme:light dark}body{font:13px/1.5 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'SF Pro Text',system-ui,sans-serif;color:#18181b;background:transparent;margin:0;padding:4px 2px}ul{margin:0 0 10px;padding-left:18px}li{margin:0 0 6px}p{margin:0 0 10px}h4{font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:#52525b;margin:16px 0 6px;padding-top:10px;border-top:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,.08)}code{font:12px ui-monospace,'SF Mono',monospace;background:rgba(0,0,0,.06);padding:1px 4px;border-radius:6px}@media (prefers-color-scheme:dark){body{color:#f4f4f5}h4{color:#a1a1aa;border-top-color:rgba(255,255,255,.12)}code{background:rgba(255,255,255,.1)}}</style></head><body><ul><li>A chat interrupted by a restart now closes the right turn; Markdown preview only shows images inside the workspace.</li></ul><h4>Also in 2.26.3</h4><ul><li>Chat polish: earlier turns no longer redraw when only the newest one changes, long commands shorten in the middle, durations keep their width as they tick, long command output stops at 12 lines with Show all, and steps read their duration and open state to VoiceOver.</li><li>A reply being written re-parses only its last block, so long replies stay smooth as they stream; teammates' names stay on one line and read "From ...".</li></ul><h4>Also in 2.26.2</h4><ul><li>Multiplayer: members can message and answer shared threads and run their own agents, shown as "Powered by ... · Flotilla".</li><li>The owner controls what each member may do, and what each thread allows, from the People menu and the thread's lock menu.</li><li>Changes apply live, without restarting a thread.</li><li>Replies to Claude/Codex running in Terminal now come with the external add-ons.</li></ul></body></html>]]></description>
